pping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra"],"id":"long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.42 (The exact gap at the largest omitted rank)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.42, p. 55, label lem:largest-false-rank-algebra","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $2\\le d<s$ and $2s<3d$. Write $W_s(E)=\\sum_{e\\in E}\\lfloor4^s/(2^e-1)\\rfloor$ for a finite set $E\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,s-1\\}$. For $u\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,d-1\\}$, put $E_-=u\\cup\\{d+1,\\ldots,s-1\\}$ and $E_+=u\\cup\\{d\\}$. Then\n$$\n3W_s(E_-)+3\\cdot2^{s+1}+2\\cdot4^{s-d}+4=3W_s(E_+).\n$$\nThe correction is independent of the common prefix $u$. For the integer-greedy rows $s\\ge5$, a right transition preserves the largest omitted rank, whereas an upper or middle transition makes $s$ the largest omitted rank in the next row.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.largest_false_rank_algebra%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.lem-largest-false-rank-algebra%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.largest_false_rank_algebra%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.Erdo